{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry your computer is giving you trouble again. I couldn't find an earlier ticket that says what \"the thing\" is, so I need a few details before I can fix it:\n1. What exactly happens? For example: it's slow or freezes, it won't turn on, it shows an error (please copy the message or send a photo), it can't get online, or apps crash.\n2. When does it happen? Is it at startup, when you open a certain app, or at random?\n3. Is this your work laptop BL-LT-0107? It hasn't connected to our network in about 12 days. Has it been off, away from the office, or unable to connect?\n4. When did you last fully restart it? Closing the lid doesn't count.\n5. Did it start after an update or after you installed something new?\nIf it's running slowly or freezing, a full restart (Start > Power > Restart) often helps for now. Once I hear back I'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "The ticket is too vague to act on (\"doing the thing again\"). I found no earlier history that explains it. User: Sofia Rossi (user_id 7, Marketing). Her account is fine: active, 0 failed logins, not blocked. Device BL-LT-0107 (Windows 11) shows offline, last check-in 2026-09-27, with the warning \"No check-in for 12 days\". Disk is fine at 54.7% free, so low disk space isn't the cause. The missing check-ins could be connected to her issue: no network, a device that won't boot, or she's just away. I've asked her for the symptoms, timing, which device, her last restart, and any recent changes. If she reports slowness or freezing, follow KB-019. If it won't power on or boot, if there are blue screens, or if the check-in problem continues, escalate to Tier 2. I haven't queued any actions.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-019"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
